[32.900122, "o", "  ⚙ bash ls /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/ 2>&1 | head -20\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 8 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: ls /usr/local/lib/python3.13/ensurepip/_bundled/ 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash ls /usr/local/lib/python3.13/ensurepip/_bundled/ 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 9 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ The problem is clear: `pip` is installed as a `.dist-info` metadata direc…\r\n[approval] bash: python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 10 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ That says \"already satisfied\" but the module is broken. Let me force a re…\r\n[approval] bash: rm -rf /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip* && python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash rm -rf /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip* && python3 -m ensu…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 11 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ Now let me verify it works:\r\n[approval"]
[32.90017, "o", "] bash: pip3 --version 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 --version 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 12 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: python3 -m pip --version 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash python3 -m pip --version 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 13 tool call(s) so far\r\n  [tools] 13 call(s) without changing a file — nudging to decide\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 13 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ Let me do a quick sanity check by installing a package:\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 install --dry-run requests 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 install --dry-run requests 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 14 tool call(s) so far\r\nEverything is working now.\r\n\r\n**What was wrong:** Your `pip` installation was corrupted — the `pip3` binary existed and pointed to the right Python, but the actual `pip` package files were missing from `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/`. Only the `.dist-info` metadata directory was present, so `import pip` failed with `ModuleNotFoundError`.\r\n\r\n"]
[32.900273, "o", "**What I did:** Removed the broken `pip` remnants from `site-packages` and ran `python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade` to reinstall it cleanly from the bundled wheel. `pip3 --version` and a dry-run `pip install` both confirm it's fully functional again.\r\n\r\n[result] role=implementor model=qwen3.6-35b tools=14 surface=76d25613e3da\r\n"]
